        <type>T &amp;</type>
        <definition>T &amp; micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::mut</definition>
        <argsstring>(const T &amp;t) noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>mut</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::mut</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const T &amp;</type>
          <declname>t</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Generic mutator to remove const qualification from any type. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the input object.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">t</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The object from which to remove const qualification. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A non-const reference to the input object.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput>mut</computeroutput> function template provides a safe and generic mechanism to remove the <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> qualifier from any type. It returns a non-const reference to the input object, enabling modification of objects that were originally declared as <computeroutput>const</computeroutput>. This utility is particularly useful in testing scenarios where controlled mutation of test data is required. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
